.TH "XmDataFieldSetMaxLength" "library call"
.SH "NAME"
\fBXmDataFieldSetMaxLength\fP \(em A DataField function that sets the value of the current maximum allowable length of a text string entered from the keyboard
.iX "XmDataFieldSetMaxLength"
.iX "DataField functions" "XmDataFieldSetMaxLength"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/DataF\&.h>
\fBvoid \fBXmDataFieldSetMaxLength\fP\fR(
\fBWidget \fBwidget\fR\fR,
\fBint \fBmax_length\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBXmDataFieldSetMaxLength\fP sets the value of the current maximum allowable
length of the text string in the DataField widget\&. The maximum allowable length
prevents the user from entering a text string from the keyboard
that is larger than this limit\&.
Strings that are entered using the
\fBXmNvalue\fP (or \fBXmNvalueWcs\fP) resource, or the
\fBXmDataFieldSetString\fP (or \fBXmDataFieldSetStringWcs\fP)
function ignore this resource\&.
.IP "\fIwidget\fP" 10
Specifies the DataField widget ID
.IP "\fImax_length\fP" 10
Specifies the maximum allowable length of the text string
.PP
For a complete definition of DataField and its associated resources, see
\fBXmDataField\fP(3)\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fBXmText\fP(3),
\fBXmDataFieldSetString\fP(3), and
\fBXmDataFieldSetStringWcs\fP(3)\&.
